! A NEGATIVE EFFECTIVE ADDRESS IS USED BY ITS MAGNITUDE -- and LOAD
! VALUE EFFECTIVE keeps its sign.
!
! An effective address goes negative only through indexing: the address
! part is "a positive unsigned field" and the index value "a signed
! 24-bit field" (Reference Manual 22-6530-2 printed p.20, PDF 23).  What
! the machine then does with it, read in the page images 2026-11-18:
!
!   printed p.21 (PDF 24): "The effective address which results from an
!     indexing operation always has 24 numeric bits and a sign.  ... only
!     the applicable part of the effective address is used.  ... The
!     effective address sign is not used in storage addressing or
!     immediate data fields. ... A negative effective address is not
!     considered to be invalid; its magnitude is used."
!   printed p.45 (PDF 48), indicator AD: "A negative effective address is
!     not invalid; the magnitude of such an address is used in the
!     operation."
!   printed p.14 (PDF 17): "The entire signed 24-bit address, with zeros
!     inserted where instructions have fewer address bits, participates
!     in the algebraic addition ... Where less than 24 bits are needed in
!     the effective address, the low-order bits are dropped."  So the
!     magnitude is formed on 24 bits FIRST and the word / half-word part
!     cut from it after (checks D, E, F, G tell the two orders apart).
!
! PER CLASS (every class that indexes goes through the same 24-bit sum):
!   VFL direct, fetch and store (A, A2, B): magnitude, p.21.
!   VFL immediate (C): p.20 (PDF 23) "The sign of the effective address
!     is ignored"; p.56 (PDF 59) "The sign bit of the effective address
!     is not used."
!   Floating point, 18-bit word address (D): magnitude, word part, p.21.
!   Direct index arithmetic, 19-bit half-word (E: LV): p.23 (PDF 26)
!     "19 bits of the effective address are used"; magnitude, p.21.
!   Immediate index arithmetic (LVI, V+I ...): NOT INDEXED -- p.24 (PDF
!     27) "the index field I is not available and no address modification
!     by indexing takes place" -- so no case here.
!   Branch (F: B): "bits 0-18 of the effective address", p.39 (PDF 42).
!   Branch relative (G: BR): p.40 (PDF 43) "the ABSOLUTE VALUE of the
!     effective address" is added to the instruction counter.
!   LVE (H): THE ONE CLASS THAT KEEPS THE SIGN -- p.28 (PDF 31): "Bits
!     0-24 of the index word specified by J are replaced by the effective
!     value plus sign"; XVLZ follows the stored value.
!   FP immediate shift (I: SHFL): amount and direction are "effective
!     address bits 0-11", p.102 (PDF 105) -- cut from the magnitude.
!   Transmit (J: TI): "Only 18 bits of each effective address are
!     used", p.30 (PDF 33); left half bit-addressed, right half 19 bits.
!   Indicator branch (L: BXVZ), I field one bit (X1 or none), p.40 (PDF
!     43); the same effAddr19 as B.  (An ARITHMETIC-indicator branch is
!     also targeted at StretchCore's look-ahead load -- not given a case.)
!   I/O (left bits 12-18, right 32-49, p.111 PDF 114: "index arithmetic
!     extends over ... the whole value field of the index word, including
!     its sign"), EX/EXIC, R/RCZ: the same helpers; NO case here.
!   Progressive indexing uses the index VALUE as the address (p.21) --
!     a stored magnitude -- and was never affected.
!   The positive path still WRAPS: a carry out of the high-order bit "is
!     ignored", pp.20-21 (K, the control).
! Hardware: TR00.722 (I-Unit Design, Mar 1960) PDF 17 -- the index adder
! has "a controlled complementer on one input, with automatic
! recomplementing ability on the output" and "end around carries": a
! negative sum comes out recomplemented, as sign and magnitude.
!
! NO IBM LISTING WE HOLD WAS FOUND TO DO IT.  Dynamic census 2026-11-18:
! the whole suite was run with the fix in place and nothing changed -- no
! CHECKED result of any deck it runs depends on a negative effective
! address.  Limits: it sees only checked results, only paths the decks
! run, and many MCP page transcriptions only assemble.  Static leads
! traced, none of them a negative register used as an I field:
!   MCP's negative queue entries ("a negative address indicates ... the
!     location to which the program should branch", C22-6728-1), the
!     LVNI,VT5,<label> sites on printed pp.216-258: stored by SV and made
!     a branch address by SVA (p.228 line 7, "SVA,VT2,1.(VP)"), which
!     takes value bits and no sign.
!   p.244 lines 41-43 "LVNI,$12,$ / V+I,$12,4.0 / B,RYSET.32": the
!     .32 entry skips p.245 line 28's LVI and reaches line 29
!     "SVA,$12,RBSP3X" -- SVA again; $12 is reloaded before any use as I.
!   ax5b test 160's I60K9 (-1.0) and I60K11 (-3.0): loaded into X0 only.
!   I00VO (all ones, negative): X0, or X2 in ibox4_rnx_run, which is not
!     then used as an I field.
! NOT traced: the zero-address dispatches (BR,0($14) p.265, BR,0.0($4)
! pp.151/153, B,0.0($1/$3/$8) ...) for the sign their registers carry;
! the untranscribed diagnostic PDFs.  So this deck is the oracle.
!
! EACH VALUE SEPARATES WRAP, MAGNITUDE, AND WORD-PART-THEN-NEGATE:
!   X1 = -(8)2000.0, X2 = -(8)2000.10, X4 = -.12, X6 = +.20,
!   X7 = -(8)2000.05, X8 = -(8)2010.41, X10 = -(8)2000.01
!   A  L(BU,64),(8)1200.0($X1)  EA -(8)600.0  -> DA        (wrap: AD)
!   A2 L(BU,8),(8)1200.0($X2)   EA -(8)600.10 -> byte 1 = 2
!   B  ST(BU,64),(8)377.0($X1)  EA -(8)1401.0 -> RB = 55
!   C  LI(BU,24),5($X4)         -7            -> 7  (wrap 16777209)
!   K  LI(BU,24),(8)777777.70($X6)  2**24-8+20 -> 12 (both)
!   D  L(U),(8)200.0($X7)       -(8)1600.05   -> word (8)1600 (FPD0);
!        word part first, then negated: (8)1601 (FPD1)
!   E  LV,$X9,(8)200.0($X8)     -(8)1610.41   -> half-word (8)1610.32
!        (22); word part first: (8)1611.0 (33)
!   H  LVE of "L(BU,8),(8)100.0($X1)"  -> value (8)1700.0, SIGN 1, XVLZ
!   I  SHFL(U),768.0($X1)       -256 words    -> left 2 (wrap: left 2046)
!   J  TI,1,(8)200.0($X1),(8)373.0($X8)  FPD0 -> RT (8)1415; receiver
!        half-word first: (8)1416 (RTF, must stay 0)
!   F  B,(8)600.0($X10)         -(8)1200.01   -> (8)1200.0, the LVI there
!        (value 32); half-word first: (8)1200.40, X11 stays 0
!   G  BR,0($X10) at (8)1300.0  +2048 half-words -> (8)3300.40 (value
!        32); half-word first: (8)3301.0, X13 stays 0
!   L  BXVZ,(8)540.0($X1)       -(8)1240.0    -> the LVI there (32)
!   RAD: no AD from the data classes.  The branches run LAST: an
!   injected wrap sends one to an uninstalled word, which ends the run.
!
! CYCLES 811, PC 455 (the control).  The injections' clock differences
! are the program's own path (AD no-ops, skipped stores, a run ended
! early); the fix moved no existing deck's pin (full suite, 2026-11-18).
! MEASURED INJECTIONS (2026-11-18; StretchExecute.bsv restored from a
! saved copy and checked with cmp after each):
!   1. the whole fix removed (the batch29 file): RA 0, RA2 0, RB 0,
!      RC 16777209, RD 0, RE 0, RH 0xff10000000000000 (wrapped value,
!      sign 0), RHX 0, RI 0, RT 0, RAD 1, RF 0, RG 0, RL 0; the run
!      ends at PC 0 after F's B; 645 clocks.
!   2. effAddr19 alone wraps: RE, RT, RF, RG, RL fail (0); PC 0; 631.
!   3. effAddr18 alone wraps: RD 0, RI 0, RAD 1; 827 clocks.
!   4. LVE stores sign 0: RH (sign bit clear, value right), RHX 0; 783.
!   5. effAddr18/19 take the word / half-word part of the wrapped sum
!      and negate THAT: RD = FPD1, RE = 33 (0x21...), RT 0 and RTF =
!      FPD0, RF 0, RG 0; 789.  (L passes: X1 has no low-order bits.)
!   6. only the indicator-branch arm (execute()'s BranchInd target)
!      wraps: ONLY RL fails (0), the run ending at PC 0; 777 clocks.
! OBSERVED, NOT INVESTIGATED (docs/NEXT.md): under 1, 2 and 6 a branch
! to an uninstalled half-word did not execute as a NO OPERATION (p.21:
! "A branch instruction with an invalid address is also executed as a
! NO OPERATION"); the run ended and the PC read 0.
!
        SLC, (8)300.0
START   LX,  $X1, XM1                ! -(8)2000.0     (1024 words)
        LX,  $X2, XM2                ! -(8)2000.10    (1024 words + 8 bits)
        LX,  $X4, XM4                ! -.12           (12 bits)
        LX,  $X6, XP6                ! +.20           (20 bits)
        LX,  $X7, XM7                ! -(8)2000.05    (1024 words + 5 bits)
        LX,  $X8, XM8                ! -(8)2010.41    (1032 words + 33 bits)
        LX,  $X10, XM10              ! -(8)2000.01    (1024 words + 1 bit)
! ---- A. VFL direct fetch, word level
        LI(BU,24), 0
        L(BU,64), (8)1200.0($X1)
        ST(BU,64), RA
! ---- A2. VFL direct fetch, bit level
        LI(BU,24), 0
        L(BU,8), (8)1200.0($X2)
        ST(BU,64), RA2
! ---- B. VFL store
        LI(BU,24), 55
        ST(BU,64), (8)377.0($X1)
! ---- C. VFL immediate
        LI(BU,24), 5($X4)
        ST(BU,64), RC
! ---- K. control: positive index, carry out of the top ignored
        LI(BU,24), (8)777777.70($X6)
        ST(BU,64), RK
! ---- D. floating point, 18-bit word address
        L(U), FPZ
        L(U), (8)200.0($X7)
        ST(U), RD
! ---- E. direct index, 19-bit half-word address
        LVI, $X9, 0
        LV,  $X9, (8)200.0($X8)
        SV,  $X9, RE
! ---- H. LVE stores the effective value plus sign
        LVE, $X14, TL
        BZB, $XVLZ, H1
        LI(BU,24), 1
        ST(BU,64), RHX
H1      SX,  $X14, RH
! ---- I. floating shift, amount from effective address bits 0-11
        L(U), FPSH
        SHFL(U), 768.0($X1)
        ST(U), RI
! ---- J. transmit, one word: 24-bit source (word part), 19-bit receiver
        TI,  1, (8)200.0($X1), (8)373.0($X8)
! ---- no AD from any data class above (the branches below would
!      no-op on an invalid address, and are last for that reason)
        BZB, $AD, F0
        LI(BU,24), 1
        ST(BU,64), RAD
! ---- F. unconditional branch
F0      LVI, $X11, 0
        B,   (8)600.0($X10)
        LVI, $X11, 3                 ! fell through: the branch was a no-op
        B,   FDONE
FDONE   SX,  $X11, RF
! ---- G. branch relative
        LVI, $X13, 0
        B,   GSITE
GDONE   SX,  $X13, RG
! ---- L. an indicator branch, whose I field is one bit (X1 or none)
        LVI, $X15, 0                 ! XVZ on
        LVI, $X5, 0
        BXVZ, (8)540.0($X1)
        LVI, $X5, 3                  ! fell through: the branch was a no-op
        B,   LDONE
LDONE   SX,  $X5, RL
        B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
        CNOP
! ---- data
        SLC, (8)600.0
DA      DD(BU,64), 72623859790382856  ! 0x0102030405060708
        SLC, (8)1200.0
TB      LVI, $X11, 1                 ! the magnitude, cut to a half-word
        B,   FDONE                   ! (8)1200.40: entered here = floored
        SLC, (8)1240.0
        LVI, $X5, 1                  ! the magnitude: -(8)1240.0
        B,   LDONE
        SLC, (8)1300.0
GSITE   BR,  0($X10)
        LVI, $X13, 3                 ! fell through: the branch was a no-op
        B,   GDONE
        SLC, (8)3300.40
        LVI, $X13, 1                 ! the magnitude, cut to a half-word
        B,   GDONE                   ! (8)3301.0: entered here = floored
        SLC, (8)1400.0
RA      DD(BU,64), 0
RB      DD(BU,64), 0
RC      DD(BU,64), 0
RK      DD(BU,64), 0
RD      DD(BU,64), 0
RE      DD(BU,64), 0
RF      DD(BU,64), 0
RG      DD(BU,64), 0
RH      DD(BU,64), 0
RHX     DD(BU,64), 0
RI      DD(BU,64), 0
RAD     DD(BU,64), 0
RA2     DD(BU,64), 0
RT      DD(BU,64), 0             ! (8)1415.0: the magnitude's word
RTF     DD(BU,64), 0             ! (8)1416.0: word part first: must stay 0
RL      DD(BU,64), 0
        SLC, (8)1600.0
FPD0    DD(BU,64), 2251799813685248  ! the magnitude's word
FPD1    DD(BU,64), 1125899906842624  ! floored word: must not be read
        SLC, (8)1610.0
        VF,  11
        VF,  22                      ! (8)1610.32: the magnitude's half-word
        VF,  33                      ! (8)1611.0: floored half-word
        VF,  44
        SLC, (8)2400.0
XM1     XW,  -(8)2000.0, 0, 0
XM2     XW,  -(8)2000.10, 0, 0
XM4     XW,  -.12, 0, 0
XP6     XW,  .20, 0, 0
XM7     XW,  -(8)2000.05, 0, 0
XM8     XW,  -(8)2010.41, 0, 0
XM10    XW,  -(8)2000.01, 0, 0
TL      L(BU,8), (8)100.0($X1)       ! LVE target: EA -(8)1700.0
FPZ     DD(BU,64), 0
FPSH    DD(BU,64), 1099511627776     ! fraction bit IBM 23
        END, START
